Given that you've got amulet reflection and think Medusa is still
alive, presumably you're invisible.  Find a way to make yourself
uninvisible and head back upstairs to kill Medusa (it won't take combat
-- just don't forget to put your blindfold on first).

Perseus's statue has a random chance of containing (cursed) boots of
levitation.  If the statue has the boots, you now have a way to cross
water.  Watch out for the eels.

If the statue doesn't contain levboots, head down to the castle, clear
it out (use your wand of cold to cross the moat, if necessary -- but be
careful and don't cross while anything hostile is nearby, to be safe),
and find the wand of wishing.  If you're impatient to finish up above
Medusa, wish yourself a good extrinsic form of levitation (I prefer
rings).

Otherwise, head down another level and clear out the Valley of the
Dead.  The various graveyard containers on that will contain a fair
amount of random stuff that might provide you with permanent or
temporary water-crossing abilities.

Good luck.

